<title>BELGIUM: EU approves SmithKline's Infantrix Hep B -- agency.</title>
<headline>EU approves SmithKline's Infantrix Hep B -- agency.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union has approved the sale of pharmaceutical firm SmithKline Beecham Biologicals multiple vaccine Infantrix Hep B in all 15 member states, Belga news agency said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>No one was immediately available at the Belgian-based firm to comment.</p>
<p>Infantrix Hep B is used to combat childhood infections of diphtheria, tetanus, whooping cough, and hepatitis B.</p>
<p>It is the first vaccine in the world to combine action against jaundice with three other vaccines.</p>
